WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.280
Speaker 1: All right. Major steps being taken&nbsp;
now. The January six committee has subpoenaed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:12.800
Trump's former White House lawyer, Patrick&nbsp;
Maloney. Patrick Maloney is a name that made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:18.240
headlines on Tuesday, in part because the closed&nbsp;
captioning could not handle the name Patrick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:25.280
Maloney. At one point it closed captioning during&nbsp;
Tuesday's hearing said patsy baloney or patsy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.880
bologna in other cases. So everybody knows the&nbsp;
name Patrick Maloney now. Patrick Maloney has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.520
been subpoenaed to testify. The Guardian reports&nbsp;
January six committee subpoenas. Former White&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.600
House counsel Patrick Maloney. Donald Trump's&nbsp;
former counsel, was a key witness to some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.080
ex-president's most brazen schemes to overturn&nbsp;
the 2020 election. Why do we care about this?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:49.360
We care about this because many of the claims&nbsp;
being made by others who have testified in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:53.920
front of the January six committee are&nbsp;
claims about what Patrick Maloney said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.360
and what Patrick Maloney told others. For example,&nbsp;
they're going to charge us with every crime in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:03.920
book or something like that. If we do this, if&nbsp;
we make this attempt to steal the election, well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:08.240
it would be really great to get him under oath.&nbsp;
Did he say that? Did he believe that? What was his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:14.000
assessment of what Donald Trump was trying to do?&nbsp;
The House Select Committee has issued a subpoena&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.120
compelling him to testify about at least three&nbsp;
parts of Trump's efforts to overturn the 2020&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:24.960
election results. The subpoena marked a dramatic&nbsp;
escalation for the panel and showed its resolve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:30.320
in seeking to obtain inside information about&nbsp;
how Trump sought to return himself to office.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.400
Mr. Chip Maloney repeatedly raised legal and other&nbsp;
concerns about Trump's activities on January 6th&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:42.240
and the days that preceded. The committee needs to&nbsp;
hear from him on the record, as other former White&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.120
House counsels have done in other congressional&nbsp;
investigations. Chip Maloney was a key witness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:52.000
to some of Trump's most brazen schemes, which the&nbsp;
select committee said in its hearings was part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:57.680
a sprawling and potentially unlawful multipronged&nbsp;
strategy, culminating in the Capitol attack.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:02.000
Chip Maloney has information about Trump's push&nbsp;
to send fake slates of electors to Congress,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:11.280
the subpoena letter said. So is he going to&nbsp;
testify? We don't know. Every indication so far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:17.120
has been that folks like Chip Maloney have no&nbsp;
interest in being put under oath and answering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.840
direct questions about what took place on January&nbsp;
six, January 5th, and the days approaching it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:29.040
He should testify. I hope he cooperates. I hope&nbsp;
he doesn't take the Steve Bannon route. And if we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:35.840
are able to. You know, the problem we're having&nbsp;
right now is you get someone at every instance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:42.960
The sequence is like this. There's the initial&nbsp;
sort of framework for the January six committee.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:47.760
Republicans say we don't like it, we're not&nbsp;
participating. Okay. So then it forces Democrats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.920
to say, are there any Republicans willing to&nbsp;
be on this committee? And Adam Kinzinger says,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:55.760
I'll do it. And Liz Cheney says, I'll do it.&nbsp;
And then Republicans say, well, look, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:00.400
they barely have Republicans on the committee.&nbsp;
Well, but that's by your choice. Then they get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:06.000
witnesses to testify. Cassidy, Hutchinson and&nbsp;
others testify. And they make claims under oath,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.960
under tremendous legal pressure, under tremendous&nbsp;
societal pressure. She now needs security on and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:18.000
on and on, getting threats and then in the media.&nbsp;
Oh well we're willing to have a different to put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:22.720
put forth her our perspective which contradicts&nbsp;
Kassidy Hutchinson's. Okay well show up and do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:27.680
it under oath. Well, they're not willing to have&nbsp;
us. Yes, they are. They said at the end of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:31.520
hearing, anyone else who has light to shed on&nbsp;
these incidents, please come forward. We would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:36.640
like you to testify. Well, where are they? It's&nbsp;
now been 48 hours. Nobody has been scheduled to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:43.360
testify as of yet. Bring them in. And so there's&nbsp;
this constant attempt to say, well, here's the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:49.120
claim made under oath. Here's something someone&nbsp;
said to someone on Twitter. They they cancel out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.720
So we don't know what the truth is. Well, no,&nbsp;
hold on a second. The statements made under oath&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:58.080
attributed to individuals should carry more&nbsp;
weight than the random musings of someone saying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:04.240
I would show up and say something different, show&nbsp;
up, take the oath and say something different,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:08.080
and then we will evaluate it. Let me know&nbsp;
on Twitter where you can find me at D&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:15.360
Pacman. Do you think any of these supposed&nbsp;
contradictions are actually going to show up and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.280
make contradictory statements under oath? Let me&nbsp;
know. We'll take a quick break and be right back.

